<%# A file picker that is also a drop target: drop files on it, tap it to open the
    system picker, or paste an image onto it. What happens on pick is the caller's —
    nothing is staged here.

    The real <input type="file"> is kept and only visually hidden. The drop handler is
    an enhancement — without the input, keyboard users and every iOS browser lose the
    picker entirely.

    The paste button is a SIBLING of the label, never inside it: a <label for> forwards
    every tap in its subtree to the file input, so nesting it would open the system
    picker instead of pasting. It renders whenever a caller passes `paste_label` and is
    hidden again by the caller on a browser that cannot read the clipboard. %>
<%# locals: (id:, label:, hint: nil, paste_label: nil, paste_error: nil,
             input_attrs: {}, zone_attrs: {}, paste_attrs: {}, error_attrs: {}) %>
<%= tag.div class: "drop-zone", **zone_attrs do %>
  <label class="drop-zone__target" for="<%= id %>">
    <span class="ph ph-camera" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span><%= label %></span>
    <% if hint.present? %><span class="drop-zone__hint muted"><%= hint %></span><% end %>
  </label>
  <%= tag.input type: "file", id: id, class: "drop-zone__input", **input_attrs %>
  <% if paste_label.present? %>
    <%= tag.button paste_label, type: "button", class: "button-small drop-zone__paste", **paste_attrs %>
    <%= tag.p paste_error, class: "drop-zone__error", role: "status", hidden: true, **error_attrs %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
